status: published
title: What this summer's heat map tells us
date: 2026-09-12
author: Grace Liu
excerpt: Blocks with five-year-old trees were up to 6°F cooler at street level on the hottest days.
image: https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1777150895644-2ca253ee1c93?w=1600&q=80
imageAlt: A young tree seedling held in two hands
---

Volunteers measured street temperatures on twenty blocks during July's heatwave. Blocks with five-year-old trees were up to 6°F cooler than those without.

We'll use the map to choose next spring's planting sites.
